<idea-plugin>
    <id>io.prismio</id>
    <name>Prismio Language Support</name>
    <vendor url="https://prismio.org">
        Prismio
    </vendor>

    <description><![CDATA[
        <h2>Prismio Language Support</h2>
        <p>
            Language support for Prismio (<code>.psm</code>) and its project
            manifests (<code>build.ums</code>) in JetBrains IDEs.
        </p>

        <h3>Prismio</h3>
        <ul>
            <li><b>Syntax Highlighting</b> - the complete keyword set, including the word operators <code>and</code> and <code>or</code>, the contextual keywords (<code>public</code>, <code>private</code>, <code>internal</code>, <code>dyn</code>, <code>spawn</code>, <code>pin</code>, <code>unique</code>, <code>Self</code>) and the FFI contract names (<code>produce</code>, <code>borrow</code>, <code>alias</code>, <code>free</code>)</li>
            <li><b>Nesting block comments</b> - <code>/* ... /* ... */ ... */</code>, matching the compiler's depth counting</li>
            <li><b>Type awareness</b> - built-in types told apart from the generic types the standard library ships</li>
            <li><b>Semantic Highlighting</b> - declarations, calls, fields, parameters, variables, constants and enum variants</li>
            <li><b>Go to Declaration</b> - Cmd+Click and Cmd+B from a name to where it is declared, across files; from an <code>import</code> to the module it names</li>
            <li><b>Find Usages and usage highlighting</b> - every name carries a reference, so usages are found and the symbol under the caret is highlighted</li>
            <li><b>Rename</b> - renaming a declaration rewrites the call sites that resolve to it</li>
            <li><b>Code Completion</b> - position-aware keyword, type and template suggestions</li>
            <li><b>Formatting, folding, structure view, find usages, documentation, spellchecking and line breakpoints</b></li>
        </ul>

        <h3>UMS manifests</h3>
        <ul>
            <li><b>Position-aware highlighting</b> - a manifest has no keywords, so block names, property keys and declaration calls are recognised by where they appear. <code>library</code> is coloured as a target kind inside <code>targets</code> and as a linker input inside <code>link</code></li>
            <li><b>Completion from the same tables</b> - suggestions come from the block you are inside, so the editor never offers a name it would then warn about</li>
            <li><b>Unknown-name warnings</b> - a weak warning naming what is valid there, never an error: UMS parses new blocks before its model learns them</li>
            <li><b>Formatting</b> - four-space blocks, <code>key = value</code> spacing, tight call parentheses</li>
            <li><b>Structure View</b> - the block tree, labelled with each declaration's first argument</li>
            <li><b>Both comment spellings</b> - <code>//</code> and <code>#</code></li>
            <li><b>New UMS Manifest</b> action, brace matching, quote handling and prose-only spellchecking</li>
        </ul>
    ]]></description>

    <change-notes><![CDATA[
        <h3>Version 1.1.0</h3>
        <ul>
            <li><b>Reformatting no longer breaks code.</b> A blanket "no space after an identifier" rule applied to `and`, `or`, `as` and `in` — which are keywords used after an expression — so Reformat Code turned <code>a and b</code> into <code>aand b</code> and <code>for i in xs</code> into <code>for iin xs</code>. Type arguments were mangled too: <code>List&lt;Int&gt;</code> became <code>List &lt; Int &gt;</code>, because <code>&lt;</code> lexes as a relational operator. Reformatting every source file in the compiler repository now preserves the token stream exactly.</li>
            <li><b>Go to Declaration, Find Usages, usage highlighting and Rename.</b> Identifiers had no references at all, so three of those silently did nothing and Cmd+Click never moved. Identifier tokens now get their own PSI element that carries a reference; resolution searches the current file first, then the project.</li>
            <li><b>Cmd+Click on an import</b> opens the module it names.</li>
            <li><b>UMS manifest support</b> — <code>.ums</code> files and <code>build.ums</code> get their own language: position-aware highlighting and completion, formatting, structure view, brace matching, both comment spellings, and a New UMS Manifest action.</li>
            <li><b>The Prismio lexer now matches the language.</b> It previously had 19 of the 30 keywords and knew none of the contextual ones, so <code>and</code>, <code>or</code>, <code>where</code>, <code>as</code>, <code>inout</code>, <code>sink</code>, <code>region</code>, <code>none</code>, <code>throw</code>, <code>public</code>, <code>private</code>, <code>internal</code>, <code>dyn</code>, <code>spawn</code>, <code>pin</code> and <code>unique</code> all read as plain identifiers.</li>
            <li><b>Nesting block comments</b>, matching the compiler's depth counting rather than ending at the first <code>*/</code>.</li>
            <li><b>Range</b> <code>..</code> is its own token; <code>0..n</code> no longer lexes as a malformed float.</li>
            <li>Built-in types are told apart from the standard library's generic types, and <code>I32</code> is no longer highlighted as a type the compiler does not define.</li>
            <li><code>_</code> digit separators are no longer accepted: the compiler's scanner has never had them.</li>
            <li><code>///</code> lines are recognised as documentation.</li>
            <li>The lexer and parser are hand-written, replacing generated JFlex and Grammar-Kit sources. Contextual keywords are not a lexical property, so a lexical grammar could not express them.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Version 1.0.0</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Initial release: highlighting, completion, formatting, live templates, structure view, folding, find usages, documentation, colour settings, spellchecking and line breakpoints</li>
        </ul>
    ]]></change-notes>

    <depends>com.intellij.modules.platform</depends>
    <depends>com.intellij.modules.spellchecker</depends>
    <depends>com.intellij.modules.xdebugger</depends>

    <extensions defaultExtensionNs="com.intellij">
        <!-- File Type -->
        <fileType
                name="Prismio File"
                implementationClass="io.prismio.PrismioFileType"
                fieldName="INSTANCE"
                language="Prismio"
                extensions="psm"/>

        <!-- Parser and Lexer -->
        <lang.parserDefinition
                language="Prismio"
                implementationClass="io.prismio.parser.PrismioParserDefinition"/>

        <!-- Syntax Highlighting -->
        <lang.syntaxHighlighterFactory
                language="Prismio"
                implementationClass="io.prismio.highlighter.PrismioSyntaxHighlighterFactory"/>

        <!-- Color Settings -->
        <colorSettingsPage
                implementation="io.prismio.settings.PrismioColorSettingsPage"/>

        <!-- Readable call colors tuned separately for light and dark schemes. -->
        <additionalTextAttributes scheme="Default" file="colorSchemes/PrismioDefault.xml"/>
        <additionalTextAttributes scheme="Darcula" file="colorSchemes/PrismioDarcula.xml"/>

        <!-- Annotator for Semantic Highlighting -->
        <annotator
                language="Prismio"
                implementationClass="io.prismio.annotator.PrismioAnnotator"/>

        <!-- Code Completion -->
        <completion.contributor
                language="Prismio"
                implementationClass="io.prismio.completion.PrismioCompletionContributor"/>

        <!-- Code Formatting -->
        <lang.formatter
                language="Prismio"
                implementationClass="io.prismio.formatter.PrismioFormattingModelBuilder"/>

        <!-- Function Body Folding -->
        <lang.foldingBuilder
                language="Prismio"
                implementationClass="io.prismio.folding.PrismioFoldingBuilder"/>

        <!-- Code Style Settings -->
        <codeStyleSettingsProvider
                implementation="io.prismio.settings.PrismioCodeStyleSettingsProvider"/>

        <langCodeStyleSettingsProvider
                implementation="io.prismio.settings.PrismioLanguageCodeStyleSettingsProvider"/>

        <!-- Comment Support -->
        <lang.commenter
                language="Prismio"
                implementationClass="io.prismio.editor.PrismioCommenter"/>

        <!-- Brace Matching -->
        <lang.braceMatcher
                language="Prismio"
                implementationClass="io.prismio.editor.PrismioBraceMatcher"/>

        <!-- Quote Handler -->
        <lang.quoteHandler
                language="Prismio"
                implementationClass="io.prismio.editor.PrismioQuoteHandler"/>

        <!-- Typed Handler for Auto-completion -->
        <typedHandler
                implementation="io.prismio.handler.PrismioTypedHandler"/>

        <!-- Enter Handler for Indentation -->
        <enterHandlerDelegate
                implementation="io.prismio.handler.PrismioEnterHandler"/>

        <!-- Structure View -->
        <lang.psiStructureViewFactory
                language="Prismio"
                implementationClass="io.prismio.navigation.PrismioStructureViewFactory"/>

        <!-- File Templates -->
        <internalFileTemplate name="PrismioFile"/>
        <internalFileTemplate name="UmsManifest"/>

        <!-- Find Usages -->
        <lang.findUsagesProvider
                language="Prismio"
                implementationClass="io.prismio.navigation.PrismioFindUsagesProvider"/>

        <!-- Documentation Provider -->
        <lang.documentationProvider
                language="Prismio"
                implementationClass="io.prismio.documentation.PrismioDocumentationProvider"/>

        <!-- Toggle Rendered View for /** documentation comments -->
        <platform.backend.documentation.inlineDocumentationProvider
                implementation="io.prismio.documentation.PrismioInlineDocumentationProvider"/>

        <!-- Spellchecking -->
        <spellchecker.support
                language="Prismio"
                implementationClass="io.prismio.spellcheck.PrismioSpellcheckingStrategy"/>

        <!-- Identifier tokens get a PSI class of their own, which is what lets
             them carry a reference. Find Usages and highlight-usages-under-caret
             are built on references; a plain leaf is never asked for any, so
             both silently reported nothing. -->
        <lang.ast.factory
                language="Prismio"
                implementationClass="io.prismio.psi.PrismioAstFactory"/>

        <!-- Rename rewrites each resolved reference through a manipulator. -->
        <lang.elementManipulator
                forClass="io.prismio.psi.PrismioIdentifier"
                implementationClass="io.prismio.psi.PrismioIdentifierManipulator"/>

        <!-- Go to Declaration: Cmd+Click and Cmd+B on a name -->
        <gotoDeclarationHandler
                implementation="io.prismio.navigation.PrismioGotoDeclarationHandler"/>

        <!-- Go to Symbol -->
        <gotoSymbolContributor
                implementation="io.prismio.navigation.PrismioChooseByNameContributor"/>

        <!-- ============================================================
             UMS manifests (build.ums)

             A separate language from Prismio: `ums/ARCHITECTURE.md` states the
             manifest DSL deliberately does not reuse the Prismio grammar, and
             the two disagree on comments, literals and structure.
             ============================================================ -->
        <fileType
                name="UMS Manifest"
                implementationClass="io.prismio.ums.UmsFileType"
                fieldName="INSTANCE"
                language="UMS"
                extensions="ums"
                fileNames="build.ums"/>

        <lang.parserDefinition
                language="UMS"
                implementationClass="io.prismio.ums.UmsParserDefinition"/>

        <lang.syntaxHighlighterFactory
                language="UMS"
                implementationClass="io.prismio.ums.UmsSyntaxHighlighterFactory"/>

        <colorSettingsPage implementation="io.prismio.ums.UmsColorSettingsPage"/>

        <!-- Colours the names the manifest system recognises, and warns about
             the ones it does not. A manifest has no keywords, so this is the
             only place that distinction can be drawn. -->
        <annotator
                language="UMS"
                implementationClass="io.prismio.ums.UmsAnnotator"/>

        <completion.contributor
                language="UMS"
                implementationClass="io.prismio.ums.UmsCompletionContributor"/>

        <lang.formatter
                language="UMS"
                implementationClass="io.prismio.ums.UmsFormattingModelBuilder"/>

        <lang.commenter
                language="UMS"
                implementationClass="io.prismio.ums.UmsCommenter"/>

        <lang.braceMatcher
                language="UMS"
                implementationClass="io.prismio.ums.UmsBraceMatcher"/>

        <lang.quoteHandler
                language="UMS"
                implementationClass="io.prismio.ums.UmsQuoteHandler"/>

        <lang.psiStructureViewFactory
                language="UMS"
                implementationClass="io.prismio.ums.UmsStructureViewFactory"/>

        <spellchecker.support
                language="UMS"
                implementationClass="io.prismio.ums.UmsSpellcheckingStrategy"/>

        <!-- Gutter Line Breakpoints -->
        <xdebugger.breakpointType
                implementation="io.prismio.debugger.PrismioLineBreakpointType"/>
    </extensions>

    <actions>
        <!-- New File Action -->
        <action
                id="io.prismio.action.createFile"
                class="io.prismio.template.CreatePrismioFileAction"
                text="Prismio File"
                description="Create new Prismio file"
                icon="/icons/prismio.png">
            <add-to-group group-id="NewGroup" anchor="first"/>
        </action>

        <action
                id="io.prismio.action.createManifest"
                class="io.prismio.ums.CreateUmsManifestAction"
                text="UMS Manifest"
                description="Create a Prismio project manifest"
                icon="/icons/ums.png">
            <add-to-group group-id="NewGroup" anchor="after"
                          relative-to-action="io.prismio.action.createFile"/>
        </action>
    </actions>
</idea-plugin>
